#*
  Base URLs of the RGD resources these templates link to.  This is the one place
  they are spelled out - every template takes its value from here.

  The Solr browse UI is served from two servers:
    - dev (hansen), where rgdweb.war and rgdCuration are deployed on the same host,
      so a relative URL resolves
    - ontomate, which serves Solr only and must point at the production webapps

  THE VALUES BELOW ARE PER-DEPLOYMENT.  This branch targets dev; the production
  branch must keep the absolute https://rgd.mcw.edu/... forms, because a relative
  URL only resolves where rgdweb.war is actually deployed.

  They can also be overridden per server, without editing this file, by a system
  property on the Solr JVM - plumbed through the "invariants" of the /browse handler
  in solrconfig.xml, which wins over anything a client sends:

    -Drgdweb.url=/rgdweb
    -DrgdCuration.url=/rgdCuration
    -Drgd.solr.url=https://dev.rgd.mcw.edu/solr

  That route needs write access to the Solr start options, so it is optional; when
  the properties are unset the values below apply.
*#
## Base URL of rgdweb.war, no trailing slash.
#if($request.params.get("rgdWebUrl") && $request.params.get("rgdWebUrl") != "")
#set($rgdWebUrl = $request.params.get("rgdWebUrl"))
#else
#set($rgdWebUrl = "/rgdweb")
#end
##
## Base URL of the rgdCuration webapp, no trailing slash.
#if($request.params.get("rgdCurationUrl") && $request.params.get("rgdCurationUrl") != "")
#set($rgdCurationUrl = $request.params.get("rgdCurationUrl"))
#else
#set($rgdCurationUrl = "/rgdCuration")
#end
##
## Base URL of this Solr server, no trailing slash.  Used both for browser-side
## lookups against the OntoSolr core and for server-side $import.read calls, which
## need an absolute URL - so this one cannot be relative.
#if($request.params.get("solrUrl") && $request.params.get("solrUrl") != "")
#set($solrUrl = $request.params.get("solrUrl"))
#else
#set($solrUrl = "https://dev.rgd.mcw.edu/solr")
#end
